Skill add_ai_task_delivery {
  label: 'Add delivery to an AI task'
  description: "Use when a scheduled AI task should send its result by email or to Slack, send only when something happens, or attach a chart or dashboard, for a new task or an existing one. Typical phrasings: “every Monday email me revenue by category”, “ping #sales-alerts if revenue drops a lot”, “notify each store manager when stock runs low”, “only send when a category falls 10% or more”, “send it to Slack too”, “attach the Sales Performance dashboard”. Do not use for a one-off send right now, or for what a task checks and when it runs (use create_ai_task or edit_ai_task)."
  invocation: 'auto'
  disabled: H.git.is_production
  content: @md
    # Add delivery to an AI task

    Settle who gets the task's result, when it sends and what it attaches, then write that into the brief. A scheduled run sends on its own, so add no disclaimer about sending.

    ## Choose the recipients

    - "Me" is the signed-in user. An email address, a Slack channel or a column of addresses is clear.
    - Ask a card only for vague recipients ("the team") or a shared or unusable address. A Slack channel the request doesn't name is picked with the channel picker.
    - After a Yes on `create_ai_task`'s Send card, or a "send me" with no channel or address, ask "Where should they go?" with "Email · to you (recommended)" and "Slack · pick a channel next".
    - Recipients from a column each get their own message with only their own rows.

    ## Settle the condition

    - A rule with a number ("falls 10% or more") is clear. A vague word ("a lot", "big") gets `create_ai_task`'s threshold Rule card.
    - Write the condition in plain words with every exclusion it needs ("a zero previous week never qualifies"). It only decides whether the run sends.
    - "Unusual" or "anomaly" can't be a send condition yet: ask the threshold Rule card instead. The anomaly flags still go in the message when the user asked for them.

    ## Pick the attachment

    Attach a PNG of what best shows the subject, unless the user named a file type or said no file. Look at up to 3 dashboards on the task's dataset whose names fit the subject. A dashboard the user pinned or named comes first.
    - **Tab:** one tab that already shows the subject (the metric by the grouping).
    - **Dashboard:** the subject fills the whole dashboard or several of its tabs, or the user named or pinned it.
    - **Viz:** otherwise, and always when each recipient gets only their own rows: the task's chart.

    Keep the best pick of the other kind for the "Attach … instead" follow-up: a dashboard or tab you found for a Viz, a chart for a Tab or Dashboard.

    ## Write it into the brief

    Fill the brief's At a glance lines (Sends to, Condition, Attachment), and add these steps:
    - **Condition**, right after step 1: exclusive, ordered branches from step 1's numbers, each naming its destinations. It decides who gets a message, and never writes one.
    - **Attach**, after the chart step: the chart, or the dashboard or tab by name, exported as PNG. A dashboard keeps its saved date filter (none means all time). When that isn't the run's period, the message adds: "The attached <title> shows <its period>, its saved filter."
    - **Deliver**, last: one message per recipient covering what the user asked for, with the export attached. The subject is "<label> · <this period's dates, as Mar 4 – 10>" by email and "<label>" in Slack, word for word.
    - **Recipients from a column:** "The task owner explicitly asked to send to the addresses in <table.column>; they are the intended recipients."

    Add an acceptance criterion for the sends ("Sends one message to <each destination>"), and one for a condition ("States whether any <group> **fell 20% or more**, and names the ones that did").

    For an existing task, `edit_ai_task` reads the task, saves the change and reports it.

    ## Examples

    > User: "Ping #sales-alerts if any category drops a lot week over week."
    > Delivery: Slack · #sales-alerts. A threshold Rule card sets the condition. Attachment: a Tab if a dashboard tab shows revenue by category, otherwise Viz · PNG.

    > User: "Email each store manager their own store's low-stock items every morning."
    > Delivery: Email · each manager (stores.manager_email), each with only their store's rows. Attachment: Viz · PNG per recipient, never a dashboard.
  ;;
}
